kinds of concerts.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.080
Right?

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.550
But that's not
something that they

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.842
would monetize because that's
part of the core business

00:05:21.842 --> 00:05:23.390
that they're offering.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:28.300
However, you start getting
into a section of APIs

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.640
which help developers--

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.140
and we're talking about
application developers--

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:38.230
which help developers build
revenue-generating apps.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:42.540
So examples like weather data,
messaging services, and Mark

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:45.480
out here will talk about
how they have achieved that.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:48.520
Think about you building
an ecosystem there.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:51.180
Today, companies
like AccuWeather

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:54.270
are becoming more
of a data company.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:56.250
That's their IP.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.350
And there are many other
application developers

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:00.900
who would like to [INAUDIBLE]
that experience of taking

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:04.050
weather data and embedding
them in different application

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.600
experiences that they're
delivering to the customers.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:13.970
That's a perfect example of why
that API should be monetized.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:16.270
So do we just take
an ad hoc approach,

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.030
or do we actually
follow a process?

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:21.010
So turns out there's a
very well thought out

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:25.060
and trusted what we call as
API monetization framework.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.450
And it's actually a very
simple five-step process.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.980
So the first one
starts with identifying

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:34.300
what are your core valuable
assets that provide

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.730
some intrinsic business value.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.553
Then, understand who the
audiences are, right?

00:06:39.553 --> 00:06:40.970
Who's really going
to be consuming

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.680
those APIs, those services?

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.870
And then comes the main part--

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.440
how do you really bundle them?

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.590
So a package or a
product bundle starts

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:52.980
to get into think
data transformation,

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:55.480
think APIs are products.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.570
So if you're the
product owner, how

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.580
do really bundle and
create a package which

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:04.013
is good for regular consumers
or direct consumers on one end,

00:07:04.013 --> 00:07:05.430
and maybe have a
different earning

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.020
mechanism for your
partners if you're

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.230
trying to grow an ecosystem?

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:12.740
And then offer, which means,
once you have a bundle,

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.650
how do you offer
up those APIs to be

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:18.310
consumed with different kind of
rate packages and rate plans?

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.900
And then last but not
the least, measure.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:23.200
This is a very important
part, because many times when

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:27.070
I ask customers, hey, how's
the API program doing, says,

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.640
the APIs are performing well.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:31.090
Well, great, but that's
only part of the equation.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.340
Are they deriving
intrinsic value?

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.870
How do you measure that?

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:37.000
Are the APIs being adopted?

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.870
Are they generating enough API
traffic from a set of partners

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:42.790
that you thought
should be doing that?

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:43.300
Right?

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:46.100
That becomes a very
important piece.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:51.980
So what does Apigee provide
from a capability perspective?

