00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:18.710
So I'm using this UI
to essentially build

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.460
what we call as API proxies.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:23.690
So think about the
slide that I just

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.900
showed where you have a
lot of enterprise assets.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:26.720
OK?

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.990
Those assets are nothing
but API that you have.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:32.870
Either you own them
organically, or they

00:11:32.870 --> 00:11:35.030
are sitting on top of
some packet application

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:39.500
that you have, or perhaps
some homegrown systems.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:44.000
Think about Apigee sitting in
the front as a facade layer.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.860
So when we represent
those APIs, we

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:48.410
