an API call which comes in.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:59.420
Execute some policies, and it
goes to a specific back end,

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.400
which is nothing but your API.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.940
So API proxy happens to be the
number one primary construct

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.740
in the Apigee Edge platform.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:13.370
Now, what happens is when
you, as the product owner,

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:17.380
in this case who owns
the portfolio of APIs,

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:20.450
you come into this screen
out here, which is what

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:22.960
we call as a product bundle.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:25.060
So within the notion
of Apigee Edge,

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:27.200
you have this
concept of a product.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.080
Think about a product
as being nothing

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:32.380
but a grouping of a
certain number of APIs.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:34.240
So let's say you have 100 APIs.

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:36.640
And you may only decide
to monetize five of them.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.490
Remember we spoke about which
APIs we monetize and which we

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:40.980
