00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:43.470
So if you think
about that bundle,

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:47.290
you could come in out here,
take that product bundle--

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:51.030
in this case, we just call it
Ad Service product bundle--

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:55.550
and this may have four or five
APIs that you want to monetize.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:57.620
So in this product
bundle definition,

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:00.950
you define what your
transaction recording policy is.

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:03.080
So it's pretty simple.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:05.390
Anytime you want to
monetize your APIs,

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.850
you want to be able to
ensure that you're only

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:13.800
monetizing those API calls where
you have a successful response.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:16.310
You may have certain
errors with API proxies.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.960
Out here, in this
definition, you're

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:20.330
saying which API
call do I really

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:23.370
want to be able to recognize
for monetization purposes.

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:26.990
So in effect, this kind of
becomes your system of record

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:30.990
for keeping track of which
APIs have been monetized.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.500
So that's the kind of
stuff we declare out here.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:36.300
Out here, we define which
specific resources within those

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:39.430
APIs you want to be
able to monetize.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:42.310
And you can add specific
custom attributes.

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:45.730
All of this level of detail
is available to the metering

00:13:45.730 --> 00:13:47.080
and billing engine.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:50.320
As API traffic is being
piped to the API platform,

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:51.850
it is picking up
what you define out

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:55.960
here in terms of enforcing
some of those aspects.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:59.910
Once you're done building a
product bundle, what you then

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:03.210
end up doing is
building a rate plan.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.850
And this is really where
you have the ability

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.130
to create different
kinds of rate plans.

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:10.980
So we spoke about some of them.

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:13.550
So essentially,
you as a provider

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:15.810
will figure out what
kind of offering

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:19.870
you want to make for this set
of APIs or this API product.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:24.380
You give it a rate plan
name, you pick the bundle,

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.240
and you pick the rate plan type.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.340
So this is an example of
what I was talking about.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:30.470
Now, you can monetize
APIs differently.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.210
You can say, well,
you're going to pay

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:35.060
a flat fee for a monthly use.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.710
I don't really
care about volume,

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.460
it's x number of
dollars a month.

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:39.433
You can pick fees only.

00:14:39.433 --> 00:14:40.850
Or you can have a
rate card, which

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:44.150
will say here's a rate card
which says how many APIs,

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.800
and for what amount.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:49.160
You can also do something
much more sophisticated,

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:51.710
where if you have a
partner ecosystem which

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.320
is getting traffic
onto your platform,

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:57.830
you can use a revenue share
arrangement where there's

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:01.340
a cut of a specific amount
of revenue, dollar amount,

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:03.080
that you as an
enterprise can ascertain

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.680
from that transaction.

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:07.370
So again, these are
various options out here.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:09.390
I'm not going to spend
time on each one of them.

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:12.230
And then you can create
the start and the end date.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:15.080
So as an API provider,
you've taken the APIs,

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.570
you've created a bundle,
and you associated that

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:20.060
to a specific rate plan.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:24.080
Once that's done, the
monetization engine kicks in.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.390
As API traffic
starts to flow, we

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:29.740
start recording based
on your preferences

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.670
those APIs which are meant
for recording purposes.

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.530
