For some, more than a
week or even a month.

00:25:25.720 --> 00:25:29.210
We're doing that at times
during the day in a second.

00:25:29.210 --> 00:25:32.770
So we had the confidence
in our data as a product

00:25:32.770 --> 00:25:34.780
and we felt it was
definitely unique to be

00:25:34.780 --> 00:25:37.780
able to offer to our end
users because we feel

00:25:37.780 --> 00:25:40.510
an API could be more
valuable for your audience

00:25:40.510 --> 00:25:42.640
if it has impactful data.

00:25:42.640 --> 00:25:44.560
And also, it has to
have an API service

00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:46.090
they can trust and rely on.

00:25:46.090 --> 00:25:49.930
So we felt we had these
with our enterprise APIs.

00:25:49.930 --> 00:25:54.930
So next we had to think about
who's our new target audience.

00:25:54.930 --> 00:25:57.650
So again, the weather
impacts everything,

00:25:57.650 --> 00:26:00.530
and everything is
powered by APIs.

00:26:00.530 --> 00:26:04.100
So we wanted people to use
AccuWeather APIs to power

00:26:04.100 --> 00:26:05.790
their ideas and business.

00:26:05.790 --> 00:26:07.340
But not just the big companies.

00:26:07.340 --> 00:26:11.060
We wanted to work with the
startups, the small businesses,

00:26:11.060 --> 00:26:14.180
the single developers,
the students, the weather

00:26:14.180 --> 00:26:16.658
enthusiasts with
just a great idea.

00:26:16.658 --> 00:26:18.200
But the problem was,
again, our sales

00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:21.620
resources were very
focused on these enterprise

00:26:21.620 --> 00:26:23.090
agreements in the space.

00:26:23.090 --> 00:26:25.010
And the contracts
were very custom,

00:26:25.010 --> 00:26:28.700
and it was very custom for
the content and the pricing,

00:26:28.700 --> 00:26:31.230
and it could sometimes
take days or weeks.

00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:33.560
So we knew we needed
something that was, again,

00:26:33.560 --> 00:26:35.688
self-serve, quick,
something that

00:26:35.688 --> 00:26:37.730
would increase the
opportunity without increasing

00:26:37.730 --> 00:26:39.080
those resources.

00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:43.038
So we started thinking, how can
we engage people on their own

00:26:43.038 --> 00:26:45.080
and get them to come to
AccuWeather on their own,

00:26:45.080 --> 00:26:49.170
without having our sale staff
consistently going after them?

00:26:49.170 --> 00:26:51.200
So that led us to our packages.

00:26:51.200 --> 00:26:53.760
And this is probably the
most interesting aspect.

00:26:53.760 --> 00:26:56.130
I'll start with saying we
love Apigee's monetization

00:26:56.130 --> 00:26:58.740
features because of the
options that we had.

00:26:58.740 --> 00:27:00.150
We actually
utilize-- I know it's

00:27:00.150 --> 00:27:02.340
a little blurry on this
screen, but we actually

00:27:02.340 --> 00:27:06.210
utilize a base fee and
a monthly CPM rate.

00:27:06.210 --> 00:27:07.800
We also offer a
free package, which

00:27:07.800 --> 00:27:09.940
we didn't offer before,
which that alone is great,

00:27:09.940 --> 00:27:11.732
because now people can
come to us, find us,

00:27:11.732 --> 00:27:13.270
test us on their own.

00:27:13.270 --> 00:27:17.490
But the base fee gives us
the ability to kind of set a,

00:27:17.490 --> 00:27:20.260
so to speak, threshold
for API request limit.

00:27:20.260 --> 00:27:22.710
And that base fee
covers up to that point.

00:27:22.710 --> 00:27:25.350
But instead of capping and
cutting off a developer

00:27:25.350 --> 00:27:28.560
as you're using the API,
we then have a CPM rate

00:27:28.560 --> 00:27:30.230
if you go over that threshold.

00:27:30.230 --> 00:27:32.250
And we loved that because
it gave the developers

00:27:32.250 --> 00:27:34.890
more freedom and flexibility
to do what they wanted.

00:27:34.890 --> 00:27:37.140
There was no hard cap
on our package limit.

00:27:37.140 --> 00:27:39.770
We didn't want to stifle
developers' creativity.

00:27:39.770 --> 00:27:42.270
The last thing you want to do
as a developer is worry about,

00:27:42.270 --> 00:27:43.860
oh, great, my
product's taking off,

00:27:43.860 --> 00:27:45.930
I hope my package
doesn't cut me off

00:27:45.930 --> 00:27:47.380
before the end of the month.

00:27:47.380 --> 00:27:50.460
So having that ability to
let them go over is great.

00:27:50.460 --> 00:27:52.440
It lets them focus on
growing their idea,

00:27:52.440 --> 00:27:56.490
not worrying about minor things.

00:27:56.490 --> 00:27:58.230
But as we went in
through this, we

00:27:58.230 --> 00:28:01.680
started to think about
what content do we expose?

00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:04.620
For AccuWeather, we had
our enterprise APIs.

00:28:04.620 --> 00:28:06.690
We intentionally did
not offer everything

00:28:06.690 --> 00:28:09.720
from our enterprise
APIs on this portal

00:28:09.720 --> 00:28:12.060
because the portal
does a lot more for us

00:28:12.060 --> 00:28:16.380
than just simply automate a
new audience experience for us,

00:28:16.380 --> 00:28:18.540
or a new target audience.

00:28:18.540 --> 00:28:21.930
It helps us act as a sales
channel to lead developers

00:28:21.930 --> 00:28:24.900
to our AccuWeather API,
and eventually, hopefully,

00:28:24.900 --> 00:28:28.050
to our sales team for a greater
partnership opportunity.

00:28:28.050 --> 00:28:30.090
So each package has
additional content

00:28:30.090 --> 00:28:32.100
as you increase
in dollar amount.

00:28:32.100 --> 00:28:36.240
But some content is still by
contacting our sales team only.

00:28:36.240 --> 00:28:38.528
It's a more premium content,
more premium experience.

00:28:38.528 --> 00:28:41.070
And we want to be able to talk
to those different partnership

00:28:41.070 --> 00:28:42.983
opportunities to see
how can we help you.

00:28:42.983 --> 00:28:44.400
Again, part of my
role, how can we

00:28:44.400 --> 00:28:45.817
help you, how can
we work with you

00:28:45.817 --> 00:28:47.520
to really leverage that API.

00:28:47.520 --> 00:28:50.520
We weren't getting rid of
our enterprise sales process,

00:28:50.520 --> 00:28:53.760
we just wanted to supplement
it, make it stronger.

00:28:53.760 --> 00:28:55.260
Another thing we
had to think about

00:28:55.260 --> 00:28:57.120
was our own lines of business.

00:28:57.120 --> 00:29:00.150
Everything internally at
AccuWeather, for the most part,

00:29:00.150 --> 00:29:01.990
runs on our own APIs.

00:29:01.990 --> 00:29:04.440
We also have a lot of other
data delivery methods.

00:29:04.440 --> 00:29:05.940
So we had to make
sure we were being

00:29:05.940 --> 00:29:09.300
consistent and fair across
the board with our data

00:29:09.300 --> 00:29:10.258
and pricing.

00:29:10.258 --> 00:29:12.300
We can't be cutting out
our own lines of business

00:29:12.300 --> 00:29:16.015
by offering a package with set
prices, but still not offer

00:29:16.015 --> 00:29:17.265
other opportunities elsewhere.

00:29:17.265 --> 00:29:19.260
So we had to be
cognizant of the fact

00:29:19.260 --> 00:29:20.820
that we're looking
at all the ways

00:29:20.820 --> 00:29:23.440
that AccuWeather brings data
to the people, and making sure

00:29:23.440 --> 00:29:25.627
that was fair and
consistent across the board.

00:29:25.627 --> 00:29:27.960
And then finally, the last
thing we had to be mindful of

00:29:27.960 --> 00:29:29.890
is what our
competition was doing.

00:29:29.890 --> 00:29:31.830
As any good business
would say, you

00:29:31.830 --> 00:29:33.840
have to always be mindful
of your competition,

00:29:33.840 --> 00:29:36.450
making sure that we're
still consistently providing

00:29:36.450 --> 00:29:39.810
that accurate weather data
forecast and a reliable API

00:29:39.810 --> 00:29:40.860
service.

00:29:40.860 --> 00:29:42.810
We want people to come
to AccuWeather because

00:29:42.810 --> 00:29:44.640
of the name and the
brand that they know,

00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:46.650
but we want them to also stay.

00:29:46.650 --> 00:29:50.460
You have to maintain
that consistency.

00:29:50.460 --> 00:29:52.170
So now that we had
our packages, we

00:29:52.170 --> 00:29:56.200
had to think about how
can we put it out there.

00:29:56.200 --> 00:29:59.520
So by partnering with Apigee, it
helped solve another challenge

00:29:59.520 --> 00:30:01.020
that we had at AccuWeather.

00:30:01.020 --> 00:30:05.250
And that was making our
APIs easy to find and use.

00:30:05.250 --> 00:30:08.832
People were unsure before how
to get to our APIs before.

00:30:08.832 --> 00:30:10.290
The most common
way was that people

00:30:10.290 --> 00:30:11.790
were seeing some
of the partnerships

00:30:11.790 --> 00:30:14.130
that we had, and potentially
had a product in their home

00:30:14.130 --> 00:30:16.600
or on their phone or
something, a widget,

00:30:16.600 --> 00:30:19.350
and they saw the AccuWeather
brand label on there.

00:30:19.350 --> 00:30:22.410
And they thought, OK,
there's data here somehow.

00:30:22.410 --> 00:30:23.100
How do I get it?

00:30:23.100 --> 00:30:24.690
And they tried to
call our sales team

00:30:24.690 --> 00:30:26.523
and get started from there.

00:30:26.523 --> 00:30:27.940
But then that's
another challenge.

00:30:27.940 --> 00:30:29.565
There's a lot of
people that don't want

00:30:29.565 --> 00:30:30.960
to talk to a sales team member.

00:30:30.960 --> 00:30:33.810
Think about if you're a startup
company or a single developer

00:30:33.810 --> 00:30:35.372
or, better yet, a student.

00:30:35.372 --> 00:30:37.080
Do you really want to
talk to a sales rep

00:30:37.080 --> 00:30:39.400
and go through a contract
and a legal process?

00:30:39.400 --> 00:30:39.900
No.

00:30:39.900 --> 00:30:43.330
You want to just go somewhere,
sign up and get started.

00:30:43.330 --> 00:30:45.870
So by having this portal,
it made it much easier

00:30:45.870 --> 00:30:47.610
for us to get the
word out there.

00:30:47.610 --> 00:30:51.940
Let people find it, try it on
their own, sign up for free,

00:30:51.940 --> 00:30:53.000
do some testing.

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:55.410
We wanted them to just
sign up, pay, and go.

00:30:55.410 --> 00:30:57.590
No delay, no days waiting.

00:30:57.590 --> 00:30:58.680
Minutes now.

00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:00.160
Get started.

00:31:00.160 --> 00:31:02.790
But once it was available, we
had to create a new marketing

00:31:02.790 --> 00:31:05.430
campaign to try to get the
word out there and reintroduce

00:31:05.430 --> 00:31:06.870
ourselves to the community.

00:31:06.870 --> 00:31:09.210
Again, people weren't sure
how to find us before,

00:31:09.210 --> 00:31:10.410
but now we're out there.

00:31:10.410 --> 00:31:11.400
We have this portal.

00:31:11.400 --> 00:31:13.048
So we want to let
people know about it.

00:31:13.048 --> 00:31:15.090
The partnership with Apigee
has been great for us

00:31:15.090 --> 00:31:17.520
because I mean, as you saw
with that commercial, that

00:31:17.520 --> 00:31:20.340
was just a one of a
three-part series, actually.

00:31:20.340 --> 00:31:25.170
We've also been on many blogs
and opportunities with them.

00:31:25.170 --> 00:31:27.030
We've also leveraged
other Google resources,

00:31:27.030 --> 00:31:30.480
like Google AdWords
and digital campaigns.

00:31:30.480 --> 00:31:32.880
And as you see from all
this cool swag pictures,

00:31:32.880 --> 00:31:35.640
we've taken it to hackathons to
kind of get the word out there.

00:31:35.640 --> 00:31:37.950
And it's been really cool
taking it to hackathons

00:31:37.950 --> 00:31:42.510
and letting the students
know, or other developers,

00:31:42.510 --> 00:31:44.940
if they want to keep using
this after the hackathon,

00:31:44.940 --> 00:31:46.622
just stay on the
site, sign up and go.

00:31:46.622 --> 00:31:49.080
So it's bringing that awareness
and engagement in that way,

00:31:49.080 --> 00:31:49.985
too.

00:31:49.985 --> 00:31:51.360
But another thing
we had to do is

00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:54.030
make sure we had a proper
presence on developer sites

00:31:54.030 --> 00:31:57.550
and resources, like
even ProgrammableWeb.

00:31:57.550 --> 00:31:58.920
Excuse me.

00:31:58.920 --> 00:32:01.080
Our presence was confirmed
in studies like this one

00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:02.760
from late 2017.

00:32:02.760 --> 00:32:04.260
And I show this
graph specifically

00:32:04.260 --> 00:32:09.180
because we launched
in about mid 2017.

00:32:09.180 --> 00:32:11.710
So this was just after
the launch of our portal.

00:32:11.710 --> 00:32:14.280
And this represents
the APIs and SDKs

00:32:14.280 --> 00:32:17.070
that readers from their site
were most interested in.

00:32:17.070 --> 00:32:20.160
And as you can see, users
had a very strong interest

00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:21.930
in AccuWeather,
but if you actually

00:32:21.930 --> 00:32:24.600
drill down into our profile
and read some of the comments,

00:32:24.600 --> 00:32:26.820
people still didn't
know how to get to us.

00:32:26.820 --> 00:32:28.370
We even saw people
saying, oh, you

00:32:28.370 --> 00:32:30.960
have to go through a sales
channel, it's very difficult,

00:32:30.960 --> 00:32:32.180
never mind.

00:32:32.180 --> 00:32:34.900
Since then, now with the portal,
we've refreshed our presence,

00:32:34.900 --> 00:32:35.650
so to speak.

00:32:35.650 --> 00:32:38.100
We've gone to these
different resources and said,

00:32:38.100 --> 00:32:39.100
we have this new portal.

00:32:39.100 --> 00:32:40.558
We've actually seen
a lot of people

00:32:40.558 --> 00:32:42.540
come through sites
like ProgrammableWeb,

00:32:42.540 --> 00:32:45.778
found us, and then moved on
and actually purchased content.

00:32:45.778 --> 00:32:47.820
So it's making sure you
have that proper presence

00:32:47.820 --> 00:32:52.317
and reputation for your
product as you get out there.

00:32:52.317 --> 00:32:54.150
So now that we felt we
had a solid new sales

00:32:54.150 --> 00:32:57.180
channel at the portal
and a solid reputation,

00:32:57.180 --> 00:33:00.230
it was important for us
to nurture our product.

00:33:00.230 --> 00:33:03.270
And that you have to
consistently keep measuring.

00:33:03.270 --> 00:33:05.010
So we do use Apigee Edge.

00:33:05.010 --> 00:33:06.580
And these numbers
are actually, I

00:33:06.580 --> 00:33:09.810
stole these or pulled these
out on Thursday of last week

00:33:09.810 --> 00:33:12.040
as I was finalizing
this presentation.

00:33:12.040 --> 00:33:15.750
So as you see, since May of
2017, that's our numbers.

00:33:15.750 --> 00:33:18.270
And with Apigee Edge, we're
able to consistently monitor

00:33:18.270 --> 00:33:19.480
growth like this.

00:33:19.480 --> 00:33:22.950
We can get snapshots of
our users in real time.

00:33:22.950 --> 00:33:25.140
It allows us to
quickly see any changes

00:33:25.140 --> 00:33:27.597
we make to our documentation
or our marketing campaigns

00:33:27.597 --> 00:33:30.180
that we potentially use to help
get the word and awareness out

00:33:30.180 --> 00:33:30.900
there.

00:33:30.900 --> 00:33:32.590
Are they being successful?

00:33:32.590 --> 00:33:34.710
So it's been very helpful
for us to kind of get

00:33:34.710 --> 00:33:38.620
that bird's eye view of those
numbers and growth and success.

00:33:38.620 --> 00:33:40.770
But also with Edge
we can drill down

00:33:40.770 --> 00:33:44.860
and get the individual analytics
for individual accounts.

00:33:44.860 --> 00:33:48.120
So with this, we can see
what APIs are they using?

00:33:48.120 --> 00:33:49.920
What APIs are they not using?

00:33:49.920 --> 00:33:52.052
Are they doing something well?

00:33:52.052 --> 00:33:53.010
Are there any problems?

00:33:53.010 --> 00:33:54.093
Because that happens, too.

00:33:54.093 --> 00:33:56.640
Are there any
abusers of our API?

00:33:56.640 --> 00:33:59.700
But also, more importantly, for
product managers and the sales

00:33:59.700 --> 00:34:02.260
team, are there any
new opportunities?

00:34:02.260 --> 00:34:04.830
We can look at clients
like this and see

00:34:04.830 --> 00:34:06.075
what APIs are they using.

00:34:06.075 --> 00:34:07.200
Are they using excessively?

00:34:07.200 --> 00:34:08.909
And we can see, is
there a potential here

00:34:08.909 --> 00:34:11.429
to reach out to them
as a new client?

00:34:11.429 --> 00:34:14.190
Because, again, we wanted this
portal to be a sales channel.

00:34:14.190 --> 00:34:15.960
Not just something
to replace, but it's

00:34:15.960 --> 00:34:18.502
something to actually help bring
us the most promising leads.

00:34:18.502 --> 00:34:20.100
Let them come on
their own, hopefully

00:34:20.100 --> 00:34:23.670
even with a small single idea,
continue to grow it with us,

00:34:23.670 --> 00:34:25.620
and hopefully be the
next big partnership.

00:34:25.620 --> 00:34:29.429
So it's really created for us
a great new lead generator, as

00:34:29.429 --> 00:34:33.810
well, as well as just providing
an additional line of revenue

00:34:33.810 --> 00:34:36.530
for us.

00:34:36.530 --> 00:34:40.780
And then finally, you have to
monitor your overall health.

00:34:40.780 --> 00:34:42.690
So with this, we can
look at our response

00:34:42.690 --> 00:34:46.719
times, the volume, the errors.

00:34:46.719 --> 00:34:50.280
We can consistently monitor
our overall health of the API

00:34:50.280 --> 00:34:52.770
and make sure we're providing
that fast, reliable service

00:34:52.770 --> 00:34:56.370
that we've been
come to known for.

00:34:56.370 --> 00:34:59.168
Because if you can't provide
that good, reliable service,

00:34:59.168 --> 00:35:01.710
why would anyone even put you
on their product to begin with?

00:35:01.710 --> 00:35:04.560
The last thing you want to
worry about as a developer

00:35:04.560 --> 00:35:08.200
is, oh no, my data provider
just failed for no reason.

00:35:08.200 --> 00:35:08.700
No.

00:35:08.700 --> 00:35:11.350
You want to focus on nurturing
your idea and your product.

00:35:11.350 --> 00:35:12.790
You want to be able to grow.

00:35:12.790 --> 00:35:16.110
But thankfully, developers
have been using us.

00:35:16.110 --> 00:35:18.030
And since our
launch, we've already

00:35:18.030 --> 00:35:20.370
seen some pretty
inspiring stories.

00:35:20.370 --> 00:35:23.760
So we actually had a
young man come to us,

00:35:23.760 --> 00:35:26.130
and he asked if he
could use our APIs

00:35:26.130 --> 00:35:28.587
to power his tortoise habitat.

00:35:28.587 --> 00:35:31.170
And what it is, as he said, his
family had a tortoise habitat.

00:35:31.170 --> 00:35:32.670
And they used our
current conditions

00:35:32.670 --> 00:35:36.500
API to actually help
control and automatically

00:35:36.500 --> 00:35:39.780
trigger in the ecosystem
within that habitat based

00:35:39.780 --> 00:35:41.140
on the outside conditions.

00:35:41.140 --> 00:35:43.800
So it's automatically adapting
using our current conditions

00:35:43.800 --> 00:35:45.040
API.

00:35:45.040 --> 00:35:47.705
We also had another
gentleman come to us and say,

00:35:47.705 --> 00:35:49.080
I have a backyard
awning, and I'm

00:35:49.080 --> 00:35:51.120
using your API to
automatically power

00:35:51.120 --> 00:35:53.370
it to open and close
based on the sky

00:35:53.370 --> 00:35:54.957
conditions and precipitation.

00:35:54.957 --> 00:35:56.790
And then he even reached
out to us and said,

00:35:56.790 --> 00:36:00.060
your API is so easy to use
and we love the accuracy.

00:36:00.060 --> 00:36:02.410
And they were both actually
just using the free trial.

00:36:02.410 --> 00:36:04.410
So just, again, a weather
enthusiast or somebody

00:36:04.410 --> 00:36:08.120
with a great idea, how easy
it was for them to go through.

00:36:08.120 --> 00:36:09.690
And then finally, at hackathons.

00:36:09.690 --> 00:36:12.050
This is actually a
picture from last fall

00:36:12.050 --> 00:36:13.920
when we were at Penn
State University.

00:36:13.920 --> 00:36:16.800
And what was great
to hear for us

00:36:16.800 --> 00:36:18.270
is, as we take
this portal there,

00:36:18.270 --> 00:36:21.780
students were coming
up to us and saying

00:36:21.780 --> 00:36:25.650
with little to no experience
working with APIs,

00:36:25.650 --> 00:36:27.450
they were able to
go on our portal

00:36:27.450 --> 00:36:29.230
because the
documentation was clean,

00:36:29.230 --> 00:36:32.040
easy to use using the portal
that we had with Apigee.

00:36:32.040 --> 00:36:34.727
They were able to just go in
there and start developing.

00:36:34.727 --> 00:36:36.810
They didn't have to worry
about how does this work

00:36:36.810 --> 00:36:38.940
and how do I do
this, they were just

00:36:38.940 --> 00:36:40.550
able to flex their
creativity and just

00:36:40.550 --> 00:36:44.140
start building some
really great ideas.

00:36:44.140 --> 00:36:46.080
So with all the success,
though, we still

00:36:46.080 --> 00:36:48.210
see even greater
potential for ourselves.

00:36:48.210 --> 00:36:50.460
We know there's even room
we can improve-- adding more

00:36:50.460 --> 00:36:52.780
content, more pricing options.

00:36:52.780 --> 00:36:54.360
So we're excited
about what we can

00:36:54.360 --> 00:36:58.840
do with Apigee to enhance this
and monetize it even further.

00:36:58.840 --> 00:37:02.460
So overall, we just
love the partnership

00:37:02.460 --> 00:37:05.040
that we've been having with
Apigee and what it's done

00:37:05.040 --> 00:37:06.750
for our developer community.

00:37:06.750 --> 00:37:09.720
To paraphrase Joel
Myers, developers

00:37:09.720 --> 00:37:13.350
are able to take our APIs and
make their products better.

00:37:13.350 --> 00:37:15.810
Because for us, that has
always been the whole goal--

00:37:15.810 --> 00:37:18.480
let developers easily put
the power of AccuWeather

00:37:18.480 --> 00:37:21.540
behind their products
and build cool things.

00:37:21.540 --> 00:37:25.190
[MUSIC PLAYING]

